@preamble let system = import("system")
args
Returns the arguments supplied to the Aiki program, excluding the interpreter
name and source filename. REPL and embedded sessions have no program arguments
unless the host supplies them.

args()

type(system.args())    # :list
===
env
Returns the value of the named host environment variable as a string. If the
variable is not set, returns [@error, :environment, msg].

env(name)

is_error(system.env("AIKI_VARIABLE_THAT_IS_NOT_SET"))    # true
===
environ
Returns the environment owned by the current Aiki runtime as a sorted list of
[@env, name, value] entries. The snapshot is independent of later host-process
environment changes.

environ()

type(system.environ())    # :list
===
set_env
Sets an environment variable in the current Aiki runtime. Future system.exec
and process.start children inherit a snapshot of this runtime environment. The
embedding process environment is not modified.

set_env(name, value)

system.set_env("AIKI_DOC_ENV", "present")    # true
system.env("AIKI_DOC_ENV")    # "present"
system.unset_env("AIKI_DOC_ENV")    # true
===
unset_env
Removes an environment variable from the current Aiki runtime. Future child
processes do not inherit the removed variable. The embedding process environment
is not modified.

unset_env(name)

system.set_env("AIKI_DOC_UNSET", "present")    # true
system.unset_env("AIKI_DOC_UNSET")    # true
is_error(system.env("AIKI_DOC_UNSET"))    # true
===
cwd
Returns the working directory owned by the current Aiki runtime. The runtime
working directory controls relative filesystem operations and process
execution without mutating the embedding Go process's working directory.

cwd()

type(system.cwd())    # :string
===
chdir
@unchecked
Changes the working directory of the current Aiki runtime. path must identify
an existing directory. Returns true on success or [@error, :io, msg]. This does
not change the embedding host process's working directory.

chdir(path)
===
exec
@unchecked
Runs command synchronously with the supplied list of string arguments. The
child process uses the current Aiki runtime working directory.

A process that starts successfully returns [@ok, stdout, stderr, exit_code],
even when exit_code is nonzero. Failure to start the process returns
[@error, :process, msg].

exec(command, args)

===
has
Reports whether the current runtime provides capability. Capability names are
Aiki symbols, not HAL identities.

has(capability)

system.has(:filesystem)    # true
===
require
Requires capability. Returns [] on success or [@error, :unsupported, msg] when
the capability is unknown or unavailable.

require(capability)

system.require(:filesystem)    # []
